A||N||2||WhiteFieroBlur||Need help with broken side mirror||||8||
Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||11-04-2001||09:15 PM||||Well I woke up this morning and going down the street to find my (Driver)side mirror is hanging off my car, I am like wha? Well I have only 1 screw left in my mirror to stick in my door the other one fell off. So I was hoping to just stick the one screw in and bolt it in real tight and maybe glue the screw in so it doesn't come out the mirror itself.<P>I was wondering if I can buy these little stud type screws that screw into the mirror in the harware store. Do you think they would have them? And do you think that just one screw with the mirror can hold? <P> It seems over time these things do come off the mirror cause it happened to my other mirror. I just got another one from a buddy off the forum. <P> Well if anyone has a complete power mirror (Black) and its on the drivers side and willing to sell me let me know. I'll buy it ASAP if I can't get this to work tomorrow. <P>||||reg||8
Z||000001||tgowens||11-04-2001||09:27 PM||||The studs in the mirror are 10mm just to let you know the size. Interestingly enough, they are the same size as the valve cover studs on a 3.4L engine (93-95 Camaro and Firebird). you could remove the inner door panel and the inner dew strip and put a bolt through into the mirror.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.whgraphics.com" TARGET=_blank>West Highland Graphics & Design</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||WhiteFieroBlur||11-04-2001||10:00 PM||||thanx for the info, I have thought about putting a screw in from inside to the mirror, but didn't think there was any room. I guess I'll find out tomorrow when I do alot of running getting the screws I need. ||||reg||1
